<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>AI Driver’s Ed for High Schools | Understanding and Working with AI</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A semester-ready AI literacy curriculum for high schools. Students are already using AI. Most have never been taught how." />
  <style>
    :root{
      --navy:#0f172a; --ink:#1f2937; --muted:#64748b; --blue:#2563eb;
      --gold:#f59e0b; --cream:#fff7ed; --soft:#f8fafc; --line:#e5e7eb;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    body{margin:0;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.5;background:#fff}
    a{text-decoration:none}
    .wrap{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}
    .hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a 0%,#1e293b 48%,#451a03 100%);color:white;padding:72px 0 64px}
    .eyebrow{font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin:0 0 14px}
    h1{font-size:clamp(38px,7vw,68px);line-height:1.02;margin:0;max-width:900px}
    .sub{font-size:clamp(19px,3vw,27px);max-width:820px;margin:22px 0 0;color:rgba(255,255,255,.88)}
    .hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:44px;align-items:center}
    .card{background:white;color:var(--ink);border-radius:22px;padding:28px;box-shadow:0 22px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.25)}
    .cta-row{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:30px}
    .btn{display:inline-block;border-radius:12px;padding:15px 22px;font-weight:800;font-size:16px}
    .btn-primary{background:var(--gold);color:#111827}
    .btn-secondary{border:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5);color:white}
    .btn-blue{background:var(--blue);color:white}
    .trust{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin-top:28px}
    .trust div{background:rgba(255,255,255,.09);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);border-radius:14px;padding:14px}
    .trust strong{display:block;font-size:22px;color:white}
    section{padding:72px 0}
    h2{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,44px);line-height:1.12;margin:0}
    .lead{font-size:20px;color:var(--muted);max-width:820px}
    .grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:22px;margin-top:34px}
    .feature{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:24px;background:white}
    .feature h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:21px}
    .feature p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}
    .dark{background:var(--navy);color:white}
    .dark .lead,.dark p{color:rgba(255,255,255,.78)}
    .split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:44px;align-items:center}
    .box{background:var(--soft);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:22px;padding:28px}
    .list{display:grid;gap:14px;margin-top:22px}
    .item{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}
    .check{color:#16a34a;font-weight:900}
    .quote{font-size:23px;font-style:italic;border-left:5px solid var(--gold);padding-left:22px;margin:28px 0 0}
    .cta-band{background:var(--cream);border-top:1px solid #fed7aa;border-bottom:1px solid #fed7aa}
    .form{display:grid;gap:12px;margin-top:20px}
    input,select,textarea{width:100%;padding:14px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:10px;font-size:16px}
    button{border:0;cursor:pointer}
    footer{padding:36px 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}
    @media(max-width:850px){
      .hero-grid,.split,.grid3{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .trust{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .hero{padding:52px 0}
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">AI literacy for secondary schools</p>
          <h1>AI Driver’s Ed for High Schools</h1>
          <p class="sub">Students are already using AI. Most have never been taught how. This semester-ready program helps teachers bring AI literacy into the classroom safely, creatively, and meaningfully.</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#preview">Preview the Curriculum</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#program">See What’s Included</a>
          </div>
          <div class="trust">
            <div><strong>Semester-ready</strong><span>Built for classroom use</span></div>
            <div><strong>Cross-disciplinary</strong><span>STEM, CTE, humanities</span></div>
            <div><strong>Teacher-friendly</strong><span>Videos, labs, assessments</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:32px">AI is already in the classroom.</h2>
          <p style="font-size:18px;color:#475569">Students use AI for homework, essays, coding, research, and personal advice. But most have never been taught what AI is, how it works, when to trust it, or when to put it down.</p>
          <p style="font-size:18px;color:#475569"><strong>That’s why we need AI Driver’s Ed.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
        <h2>AI is not just another classroom technology.</h2>
        <p class="lead">It is cognitive technology. It changes how students write, think, research, create, and judge what is true. The question is no longer whether students will use AI. The question is whether they will learn to use it well.</p>

        <div class="grid3">
          <div class="feature">
            <h3>Use AI critically</h3>
            <p>Students learn to question outputs, identify weak reasoning, and ask for opposing views.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature">
            <h3>Stay the author</h3>
            <p>The program emphasizes human judgment, voice, responsibility, and creative ownership.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature">
            <h3>Understand the tool</h3>
            <p>Students build a conceptual model of what AI is, what it is not, and why that matters.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="program" class="dark">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The program</p>
          <h2>A complete AI literacy pathway for high school classrooms.</h2>
          <p class="lead">Understanding and Working with AI is designed to move students from casual AI use toward thoughtful AI fluency.</p>
          <div class="quote">“AI is designed to agree with you. That’s a problem. If you don’t actively ask for the opposing view, you won’t get it.”</div>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0">What teachers receive</h3>
          <div class="list">
            <div class="item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Two-volume student curriculum: foundations, practice, society, and the future</span></div>
            <div class="item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Video lessons and podcast companions for each chapter</span></div>
            <div class="item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>AI experiments, classroom activities, and discussion prompts</span></div>
            <div class="item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Teacher supports for STEM, CTE, social studies, and language arts contexts</span></div>
            <div class="item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>A practical framework for safe, responsible, creative AI use</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Who it’s for</p>
          <h2>Built for educators who know AI cannot be ignored.</h2>
          <p class="lead">Use it as a semester course, an interdisciplinary unit, a professional development anchor, or a foundation for district-wide AI literacy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid3" style="grid-template-columns:1fr; margin-top:0">
          <div class="feature"><h3>High school teachers</h3><p>Bring AI literacy into real classrooms without starting from scratch.</p></div>
          <div class="feature"><h3>Curriculum leaders</h3><p>Provide a coherent framework across departments and grade levels.</p></div>
          <div class="feature"><h3>Administrators</h3><p>Respond constructively to AI use instead of relying only on bans and detection tools.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="preview" class="cta-band">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
          <h2>Preview the AI Driver’s Ed curriculum.</h2>
          <p class="lead">Request a preview and see whether this program is a fit for your students, teachers, or school.</p>
          <p style="color:#64748b">You can connect this form to your preferred email or CRM, or replace it with a direct link to your sample chapter.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="box-shadow:0 12px 35px rgba(15,23,42,.12)">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;font-size:24px">Request a curriculum preview</h3>
          <form class="form" action="#" method="post">
            <input name="name" placeholder="Name" required />
            <input name="email" type="email" placeholder="Email" required />
            <input name="school" placeholder="School or organization" />
            <select name="role">
              <option value="">Your role</option>
              <option>Teacher</option>
              <option>Administrator</option>
              <option>Curriculum director</option>
              <option>Parent / homeschool</option>
              <option>Other</option>
            </select>
            <textarea name="message" rows="3" placeholder="What are you looking for?"></textarea>
            <button class="btn btn-blue" type="submit">Send Me the Preview</button>
          </form>
          <p style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:0">Replace this placeholder form action with your site’s form handler, or embed your existing form service.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:860px">
        <p class="eyebrow">The larger vision</p>
        <h2>Students do not just need access to AI. They need AI fluency.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">The goal is not to make students dependent on AI. The goal is to help them become thoughtful human beings who can use powerful tools with judgment, creativity, and care.</p>
        <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:center">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#preview">Preview the Curriculum</a>
          <a class="btn" style="border:2px solid #cbd5e1;color:#1f2937" href="https://understandingai.ai/pocketlab">Learn More</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap">
      © UnderstandingAI.ai · Conceptual Academy
    </div>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>
